invariant: INV-16
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: table_select copies the one entry its index names, where it read
  all sixteen and kept one by a mask. The index is a digit of the private
  exponent, so the address the copy reads depends on it, which an
  attacker who shares the data cache can watch. Every byte still comes
  out the same and no branch is added, so the vectors, the equivalence
  test and the branch count all pass. inv-16-rsa-table-read refuses a
  subscript of the table that is no constant and no loop counter.

--- old
        for (size_t i = 0; i < k; i++) {
            o[i] = (o[i] & ~mask) | (table->powers[entry][i] & mask);
        }
--- new
        (void)mask;
        memcpy(o, table->powers[index], k * sizeof(uint64_t));
